We eat the last piece of fruit tart.
The tart is really very delicious.
Afterwards, the beautiful evening is slowly coming to an end.
I thank Nele for the wonderful food and the great company.
I tell her that unfortunately I have to go now.
It is already late and I stand up.
To leave, I put on the backpack.
Nele accompanies me to the door and smiles.
She promises me that she will visit my flat next time.
"Yes, I will cook for us then," I answer happily.
We say goodbye at the door.
We hug each other briefly.
Then I go outside.
The late spring air is still pleasantly mild.
I walk to the U-Bahn.
On the way, I think about the evening.
It is a great feeling.
Nele and I are real friends now.
